   "tuning": [],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "Thm:PermLB",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Let $\\nu$ be an $\\MAB$ instance with unique best arm $a^*$ ... If $\\Alg$ is $\\delta$-correct over $\\bS_n(\\nu)$ then ... $\\Exp_{\\pi \\sim \\bS_n}\\Exp_{\\pi(\\nu),\\Alg}[T] \\geq \\sup_{\\eta \\in [\\delta, 1/4]} (\\eta - \\delta) \\log(1/4\\eta)  \\sum_{b \\neq a^*}\\tau_b$. In particular, if $\\Alg$ is $\\delta \\le 1/8$-correct, then $\\Exp_{\\pi \\sim \\bS_n}\\Exp_{\\pi(\\nu),\\Alg}[T] \\gtrsim  \\sum_{b \\neq a^*}\\frac{1}{\\KL(\\nu_{a^*},\\nu_{b}) +\\KL(\\nu_{b},\\nu_{a^*})}$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "General form: sup_{eta in [delta,1/4]} (eta-delta) log(1/(4 eta)) sum_{b != a*} tau_b. For Gaussians gives sum Delta_b^{-2}. Lower bound is averaged over permutations."
  },
